## What each ticket asks (re-read each by Jira GET, STANDING LINE 1; say in STATUS (Corrections) where it differs)
1. **HPSMPOC-422.** Gate B981 found that the not-applicable variant of a question block (`QuestionBlock.tsx` line 45) carries its own `id` and that removing it leaves every web unit row green: the existing anchor row (`AssessmentScreen.restyle.test.tsx` lines 137-148) builds its expected ids from the questions `resolveVisibility` marks SHOWN and then counts `[id^="q-"]` against that, with the seeded profile, where no shown question is not applicable. Done when (the ticket's): the id is pinned by a row that turns red when it is dropped, OR the branch is shown unreachable, OR the item is recorded as declined. **Reachability (MEASURED BY THE DRAFTER from the files, NOT run): reachable.** In the ruleset the screen runs on (`ruleset.synthetic-structural.json`, 4 questions), `Q-S1-002` has `showWhen` `Q-S1-001 in [no, partial]` and `applicableWhen` `P-synthetic-kind neq beta`; the seeded profile is `alpha` (`session.ts` line 84). So profile `beta` plus an answer `no` on `Q-S1-001` makes `Q-S1-002` shown and not applicable. The reducer actions exist: `{ type: "setProfile", fieldId, optionId }` (`session.ts` line 108) and `{ type: "setAnswer", questionId, optionId }` (line 109). **The row (build it in this shape; use the file's own helpers `seed`, `SIGNED_IN`, `quollridge`, `CustomerProvider`, never new ones):** (a) `seed([SIGNED_IN, {setProfile P-synthetic-kind beta}, {setAnswer Q-S1-001 no}])`; derive the expected set the way the existing row does, from the state after those actions (`[...].reduce(reducer, initialState()).assessment`, then `resolveVisibility(ruleset, rawAnswers(a.responses), a.profile)`): `na = orderedQuestions(ruleset).filter((q) => v.shown[q.id] && !v.applicable[q.id])`; assert `na.length` is greater than 0 (so a ruleset change says so instead of passing on nothing); render `<CustomerProvider value={quollridge}><AssessmentScreen /></CustomerProvider>`; for each `q` in `na`: `container.querySelector('[id="q-' + q.id + '"]')` is not null AND that block holds no radio, no text area and no select (it is the not-applicable variant: assert by `querySelectorAll("input, textarea, select")` length 0, a handle with no words); and `container.querySelectorAll('[id^="q-"]')` has length equal to the number of SHOWN questions (one anchor per block, the not-applicable block included). (b) a control row: the same actions but profile `alpha` gives `na.length` 0, and the block for `Q-S1-002` holds at least one radio (so the profile, not the markup, is what flips it). Both rows are GREEN at the pin (a pin gap, not a defect: say so, they are controls on the product and become red only under plants q1 and q3 below). Row names carry no ticket key and no B-number. **If the variant cannot be drawn in the real screen (the render shows no `q-Q-S1-002`, or the profile will not change), do not force it: record "unreachable" with the program output in STATUS, build no row, make no commit 1, and say so in the last line.**
2. **HPSMPOC-423.** Gate B989 measured the constant (`remediation-store.ts` line 22, `SHOWS_NOTHING`) against all 1,112,064 scalar values: the list counts as empty the evidence made only of white space and the 188 listed characters; **3990 further code points are Unicode white space or default-ignorable and are not in it** (U+0085 (1), U+FFF0-U+FFF8 (9), U+1BCA0-U+1BCA3 (4), U+1D173-U+1D17A (8), U+E0080-U+E0FFF (3968)). The drafter re-ran the measurement (MEASURED, Node v26.8.1, ICU 78.3, Unicode 17.0, the class extracted from the file at `d0eff4ca` by program): |A| (the class) 213, |B| (`\p{White_Space}` or `\p{Default_Ignorable_Code_Point}`) 4199, **B minus A = 3990 = those same five ranges (control: the printed ranges equal the ticket's)**, A minus B = 4 (U+2800 and U+FFF9-U+FFFB, which are listed on purpose because they draw nothing though not default-ignorable). `"\u0085".trim().length` is 1 and `/\s/.test("\u0085")` is false (JavaScript `\s` and `trim()` miss U+0085). **THE DECISION (default, stated as Q-1 in the drafter report, and in force unless the stamp says otherwise): ADD the four ranges U+0085, U+FFF0-U+FFF8, U+1D173-U+1D17A, U+E0080-U+E0FFF; LEAVE U+1BCA0-U+1BCA3 OUT.** Why: the ticket says U+1BCA0 draws a visible box in Chromium (the gate saw it), so evidence made of it shows something; whether it counts as blank is "a scope call that is not made here" and stays the product owner's. **The property first (the closed-list rule):** *evidence is blank when every code point of it, after trim(), either is white space (`\s` or U+0085) or draws no glyph on its own.* **At least these** are in the class after your edit: everything already there (lines 20-22 at the pin) plus U+0085, U+FFF0-U+FFF8, U+1D173-U+1D17A, U+E0080-U+E0FFF. **Any other shape: prove it meets the property (no visible glyph on its own) or STOP.** Implementation (the edit is exactly this and no more): in the single explicit `u`-flag class of line 22, add `\u{85}`, `\u{FFF0}-\u{FFF8}`, `\u{1D173}-\u{1D17A}` and `\u{E0080}-\u{E0FFF}`; keep the existing members byte-equal; keep the `^[...]*$` frame and the `u` flag. The result is the ONLY changed line in the file apart from ONE added ASCII comment line above it naming what was added and that U+1BCA0-U+1BCA3 stay out because they draw a box (lines 20-21 stay byte-equal). Do NOT use `\p{Cf}` or `\p{Default_Ignorable_Code_Point}` (they would also blank U+1BCA0 and, for `\p{Cf}`, marks that draw: the file's own comment says why). **Scope (unchanged, the product owner's 2026-10-31 stamp answer to Q-1 of the first blank-evidence build):** the blank test applies to "Verified complete needs an evidence reference" only; do not rewrite what is stored for the other three states, do not touch the owner. **Known consequence to state in STATUS (do not "fix" it; it is HPSMPOC-424's question):** `parseEntry` re-runs `checkEntry`, so a stored Verified-complete entry whose evidence is only one of the newly listed characters is now dropped on read, and `parseRegister` then returns null for the whole register; only this tab's sessionStorage could ever hold one (an older build could write it).
   **Rows (`remediation-store.test.ts`, ADD lines only, 0 removed):** (a) **one row per range:** insert four entries into the `NO_GLYPH` table (lines 53-60) as new lines between line 59 and the closing `];` of line 60 (line 59 already ends with a comma, so no existing line changes): `["the next line (NEL)", 0x85, 0x85]`, `["the interlinear object marks", 0xfff0, 0xfff8]`, `["the musical beam and tie format controls", 0x1d173, 0x1d17a]`, `["tag characters beyond the first block", 0xe0080, 0xe0fff]`. The existing `it.each(NO_GLYPH)` loop already walks EVERY code point of each range, alone and tripled, and expects the same refusal object (`message: NEEDS_EVIDENCE`, `field: "evidence"`), so each entry is a row that turns red when ANY code point of its range is dropped. (b) **a mixed row:** white space and the new characters together (for example `" \u{85} "`, `"\u{FFF0}\u{1D173}\u{E0080}"`, `"\t\u{E0FFF}\n\u{FFF8}"`) refused for Verified complete. (c) **negative controls (GREEN at the pin and after):** a character that draws, beside each new range, is NOT blank: `"a\u{85}"`, `"\u{FFF0}a"`, `"a\u{1D173}"`, `"\u{E0080}a"`; and characters just outside the ranges that draw: `"\u{1D172}"`, `"\u{1D17B}"` (musical combining marks), `"\u{FFFC}"`, `"\u{FFFD}"`; each accepted with `{ ok: true, entry: ... }` exactly as the existing accept row (line 79-83) writes it. The seat measures with Node that none of the neighbours is `\p{Default_Ignorable_Code_Point}` or `\p{White_Space}` and prints it; one that is, is dropped and named. (d) **the left-out range (Q-2 default: yes, pin it):** one row that `"\u{1BCA0}"` and `"\u{1BCA3}"` are ACCEPTED for Verified complete, with a comment line "a visible box: kept out on purpose, widen only on the product owner's word". It is GREEN at the pin; its plant (p5) turns it red. (e) the same new characters for state `In progress` stay accepted (the rule is for Verified complete only): one `it.each` over the three other states with `"\u{85}"` and `"\u{E0080}"`. Use `\u{...}` escapes only (the file's style and lint accept them; ASCII only in every added line); at most one short comment line per new group. **Before the product edit, show the new rows RED on the pin's product:** (a), (b) red; (c), (d), (e) green controls.
3. **Proof instrument for the property (scratch only, not committed, print the result):** a Node program that extracts the class from your edited line 22 and sweeps all scalar values: A minus B must be exactly U+2800 and U+FFF9-U+FFFB (4), and B minus A must be exactly U+1BCA0-U+1BCA3 (4). Control: the same program on the pin's line prints B minus A = 3990 and the five ranges above (if it prints anything else, say what and STOP). Print Node's version and ICU version beside it; the CI runner's Node is 24 and may carry different Unicode data: say so in NOT TESTED.

